 mice were  plagued by latency issues and nobody  wanted to use them for gaming if you're  playing games at the highest level of  competition there's no way in hell you  want a laggy mouse pro players just  couldn't trust them so to combat this  issue logitech developed lightspeed  lightspeed as a technology has  fundamentally changed the game in terms  of  what is possible on the pro stage now  logitech claimed that their new light  speed technology offered a one  millisecond response time a speed so  fast that it could potentially be more  responsive than some wired mice now some  people were skeptical of this naturally  but as it turns out  logitech wasn't kidding tech review  channels like linus tech tips were  pretty quick to confirm that gaming mice  using lightspeed do in fact respond  faster than some wired mice and although  they weren't able to physically test the  transmission time they did confirm that  there is no noticeable difference  between a wired mouse and a mouse using  logitech's wireless light speed  technology what we can take away from  our experiment is that at least for  logitech we have validated their  position that anyone who claims to be  able to tell the difference between  their wired and wireless mice is either  imagining it or full of  and that is all that the world of  esports needed to hear not to mention  the fact that according to logitech the  g-pro boasted 48 hours of battery life  with the rgb lighting on and 60 hours  with the lighting off and that you could  charge it back to full in just two hours  so with all of this good stuff to say  about the g pro and its performance it  begs the question why would you use  anything else well that's what's so  interesting about mice while this  lightweight wireless low latency beast  is impressive it's not guaranteed to  make you better at games mice aren't  just science there's a splash of romance  to them over time comfort trumps all and  for people like me who would die for  their 